  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bell Textron has $2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 817 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $2.5M. Obligations rose up 33.9% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a multi-year increase: FY21 was $349M, FY22 was $307M, FY23 was $985M, FY24 was $1.2B, FY25 was $1.5B, and FY26 is $2B. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $2B so far in FY2026. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market by NAICS, with $1.8B in obligations. Secondary markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing with $206M and Scale and Balance Manufacturing with $1.6M. Smaller markets include Engineering Services with $635K and Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services with $761K. The Department of the Interior, Department of Justice, Department of Transportation, and Department of Energy are smaller buyers, with obligations of $53.2M, $612K, $135K, and $58.5K respectively. The current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Bell Textron's federal business changed year over year?",
        "body": "Bell Textron's obligations rose up 33.9% year over year. The company moved from $1.5B in FY25 to $2B in FY26. Fiscal-year history shows growth from $349M in FY21 and $307M in FY22 to $985M in FY23 and $1.2B in FY24. FY26 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Bell Textron's biggest agency customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $2B for Bell Textron in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior obligated $53.2M, and the Department of Justice obligated $612K. The Department of Transportation obligated $135K, and the Department of Energy obligated $58.5K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Bell Textron make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Bell Textron has $2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 817 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2.5M. Fiscal totals increased from $1.5B in FY25 to $2B in FY26, and obligations rose up 33.9% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Bell Textron?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is Bell Textron's largest buyer, obligating $2B in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior obligated $53.2M, the Department of Justice obligated $612K, the Department of Transportation obligated $135K, and the Department of Energy obligated $58.5K."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Bell Textron sell to the government?",
      "a": "Bell Textron sells aircraft and aircraft-related products and services to the government. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Bell Textron with $1.8B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Other identified markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing with $206M, Scale and Balance Manufacturing with $1.6M, Engineering Services with $635K, and Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services with $761K."
